\ The calling half of aot_inline_error_frames_image.
\
\ Expansion erases the call to `inner`, so at run time nothing is left to push its frame. The only
\ record of where that code came from is the run the expansion pass wrote over this body, and in a
\ runtime-image binary that run has to have travelled in the image.

use "aot_inline_error_frames_image_lib.1z" ;

outer: ( s v -- n ) [ inner 0 + ] ;
